<title>UK: Daiwa in deal with Vietcombank - report.</title>
<headline>Daiwa in deal with Vietcombank - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Vietnamese bank Vietcombank has signed a memorandum of understanding with Japan's Daiwa Securities Co Ltd to set up Vietnam's first joint venture securities business, a British newspaper reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Daiwa Securities said last year that it had received permission to set up a representative office in Hanoi, and the Financial Times said that office had opened on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted a Daiwa official as saying the business would focus on helping Vietnam prepare companies for listing on an eventual bourse, including the privatisation of state-owned companies.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44-171-542-7717</p>
</text>
